WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:07.680
The creature let out an unmistakable squeal&nbsp;
of rage as Stimulus Y835 took effect. Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:13.800
Kristiansen pressed his face up against the glass,&nbsp;
eager to see the results. It had to work this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:19.320
time, it simply had to. He was certain that this&nbsp;
attempt would make all the other failures worth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:26.340
it, and he’d once again prove the Foundation’s&nbsp;
faith in him to be well-placed. SCP-5683 shrieked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:32.220
a loud, insect-like sound that would have normally&nbsp;
made the blood run cold of anyone that heard it.&nbsp;

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:39.720
But to Doctor Kristiansen, it was like music – a&nbsp;
monster’s dying fanfare to mark his success. Soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:47.100
he’d be the researcher who neutralized not one,&nbsp;
but two tenacious, highly adaptable anomalies. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.840
senior researcher could feel his heart racing&nbsp;
as the deadly giant spider started to twitch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:58.200
then burst into two identical entities.&nbsp;
The pair of arachnid anomalies had reacted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.120
much like the results of the tissue sample&nbsp;
test conducted earlier, dividing into two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:08.460
separate organisms. Kristiansen held his breath&nbsp;
– the tissue samples had destroyed each other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:14.280
attacking and injecting the other with lethal&nbsp;
doses of venom. Surely, he reasoned, duplicating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:21.060
SCP-5683 into two would have the same result…
His heart sank as he watched one of the spider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:27.000
creatures – the duplicate – perish almost&nbsp;
immediately. As it often did when presented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:34.500
with human prey, SCP-5683 attacked using its&nbsp;
mandibles and impaled its copy with its front legs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:40.620
to pin it in place. The clone had bitten back,&nbsp;
with Doctor Kristiansen already knew would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:47.460
granted SCP-5683 an immunity to its own venom.
Its powers of adaptation were fiercely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:53.460
frustratingly efficient, and nothing demonstrated&nbsp;
this more than the intense reaction from the man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:59.580
tasked with destroying it. Doctor Kristiansen&nbsp;
hurled the nearest object – a coffee mug –&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:04.560
at the glass window of the observation room,&nbsp;
overlooking the testing chamber. He pounded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.900
his fist against the glass, hardly with the&nbsp;
required force to cause damage, but enough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:16.020
send pain shooting down Kristiansen’s wrist, which&nbsp;
then nestled in his forearm; a reminder that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:23.280
experiment, like the others, had failed.
“Why can’t I destroy you?” he muttered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.560
through clenched teeth, looking with hatred&nbsp;
at the enormous spider in the chamber below.&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.180
The directive had reached him the day&nbsp;
immediately after New Years’ Day 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:39.300
and straight from a member of the O5 Council, no&nbsp;
less. Their message expressed how impressed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:45.300
Council was with Doctor Kristiansen’s success with&nbsp;
the Doomsday Clock project, and how favorably his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:50.700
name had been mentioned in Council meetings. This&nbsp;
boded well for the ambitious Foundation doctor;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:56.820
he’d been hoping to snag the Director position&nbsp;
at Site 04 now that Director Bray had retired.&nbsp;

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:02.100
But there was one more test from the O5&nbsp;
Council. They wanted Doctor Kristiansen to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:09.660
use the knowledge garnered during his previous&nbsp;
success to solve the SCP-5683 problem. If he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:15.120
could successfully complete that assignment, it&nbsp;
would be his ticket to being promoted. With the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:20.940
comfy role of Site Director and all its perks in&nbsp;
mind, Doctor Kristiansen accepted the assignment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:29.280
from the Council to deal with SCP-5683.
SCP-5683 was quite the beast, not an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:34.380
anomaly for those with intense arachnophobia.&nbsp;
The huge spider-like organism was extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:39.840
hostile towards humans, and had to be kept in a&nbsp;
constant state of medical sedation. Otherwise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.980
it would relentlessly attempt to breach&nbsp;
containment and slaughter any and all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:50.880
personnel in its path. What had made SCP-5683 such&nbsp;
a problem for the Foundation was the creature’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:57.060
ability to rapidly regenerate damage as well&nbsp;
as modify its own body in reaction to threats.&nbsp;

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:03.960
Much like a certain, particularly Hard to Destroy&nbsp;
Reptile, the spider-like entity could adapt itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:09.420
to become more resistant to any danger posed to&nbsp;
it. And, of course, this meant that the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:14.880
needed this dangerous creature eradicated. The&nbsp;
frequent containment breaches and sheer number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:20.220
of casualties caused by the arachnid anomaly were&nbsp;
significant enough to cause an increasing drain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:26.640
on the SCP Foundation’s resources. So, with the&nbsp;
termination order coming from the very top, the O5&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:34.440
Council themselves, Doctor Kristiansen was tasked&nbsp;
with overseeing the neutralization of SCP-5683.&nbsp;

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:39.900
During an initial deliberation, Doctor&nbsp;
Kristiansen met with Researchers Miles and Hall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:45.600
Junior Researcher Silva, and Security Chief&nbsp;
Aday to discuss earlier attempts to terminate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:52.080
SCP-5683. The new head of the termination project&nbsp;
was perturbed to learn that the research team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:57.180
had little in the way of useful information to&nbsp;
offer, beyond what the Foundation already knew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:02.880
about the creature. But Kristiansen decided some&nbsp;
basic stress testing would at least be a start.&nbsp;

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:09.000
After a successful tissue sample test,&nbsp;
wherein some of SCP-5683’s genetic material&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:13.920
was incinerated, Doctor Kristiansen tried&nbsp;
to simply destroy the spider with fire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:21.300
An understandable response, to say the least.&nbsp;
However, exposing SCP-5683 to temperatures of 850&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:27.060
degrees Celsius for just thirty seconds didn’t&nbsp;
quite yield the easy victory he’d hoped for.&nbsp;

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:32.700
The arachnid thrashed about and screeched in&nbsp;
reaction to the heat, only to rapidly develop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:37.800
a form of armor plating covering its entire&nbsp;
body. The armor was comprised of an unknown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:43.920
unidentifiable substance, but it was&nbsp;
enough to prevent SCP-5683 from combusting.&nbsp;

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:48.180
Reconvening with the rest of the team,&nbsp;
Doctor Kristiansen hid his pride,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:53.520
assuring everyone he was just trying to establish&nbsp;
a baseline during the previous test. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.520 --> 00:06:00.600
he hadn’t believed that terminating SCP-5683&nbsp;
with fire would be a success, or so he claimed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:06.420
hiding how much he’d longed for an easy solution&nbsp;
so he could snatch up the vacant Site 04 Director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:12.360
position. But to ensure the others, Kristiansen&nbsp;
explained that he’d requisitioned some anomalous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:17.220
materials from the O5 Council, that they’d&nbsp;
be using in their next termination attempts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:22.500
Nothing that was anomalous enough to require&nbsp;
containment, but toxic enough that they presented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:28.800
a few options for destroying SCP-5683.
“Just for logging purposes, sir,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:34.200
may I inquire about the specific substances we’re&nbsp;
shipping in?” Junior Researcher Silva had asked.&nbsp;

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:40.620
“Of course. Y220, Y835, and Y43,” Doctor&nbsp;
Kristiansen quickly recounted them all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:44.220
from memory. “I’m told they should&nbsp;
be arriving within the week. I expect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:48.720
each would be enough to do the job, but it’s&nbsp;
best to hedge our bets. This spider doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:53.160
compare to the lizard, I’ll tell you that.”
Junior Researcher Silva seemed to take an interest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:59.760
in what Doctor Kristiansen had just alluded to:&nbsp;
his previous work with ‘the lizard’. He probed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:04.920
further about it, and Kristiansen gave a solemn&nbsp;
response. The aspiring Foundation Doctor recalled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:10.560
an incident from a few years earlier during&nbsp;
his experimentation with SCP-682. Some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:15.300
methods Doctor Kristiansen had opted to employ in&nbsp;
an attempt to destroy the Hard to Destroy Reptile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:21.420
had led to a severe containment breach. When&nbsp;
describing it, he used the word ‘unpleasant’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:26.280
perhaps out of guilt at how many personnel had&nbsp;
lost their lives due to his actions. Brushing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:33.300
the topic aside, he urged his team to get on with&nbsp;
testing the new anomalous stimuli on SCP-5683.&nbsp;

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:38.220
Stimulus Y220 initially showed some&nbsp;
promise: during a Tissue Sample Test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:44.820
it successfully converted part of SCP-5683&nbsp;
into glass, which then violently exploded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:49.920
leaving nothing behind. But attempts to use&nbsp;
it to neutralize the creature itself quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:55.380
quashed those promising results. Within nine&nbsp;
seconds of being exposed to Stimulus Y220,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.380 --> 00:08:02.520
SCP-5683’s body rapidly turned into glass. Around&nbsp;
eighty percent of its arachnid mass proceeded to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:07.920
explode, shattering in all directions, sending&nbsp;
clear shards showering over the testing chamber.&nbsp;

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:12.900
As he watched, Doctor Kristiansen allowed himself&nbsp;
to believe that this was mission accomplished,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:20.160
that he’d successfully terminated SCP-5683.&nbsp;
But his celebration was premature; the spider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:26.220
quickly began reconstituting itself, its body&nbsp;
regenerating within the space of thirty seconds.&nbsp;

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:33.420
After testing with both Stimuli Y220 and Y835,&nbsp;
Doctor Kristiansen’s frustration seemed to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:38.340
increasing with each failed attempt. He knew&nbsp;
his promotion was within reach. And as far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:44.460
as he could remember, he’d done good work with&nbsp;
damaging SCP-682. Why should eradicating this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:50.820
anomalous spider be any different? However, it&nbsp;
was the test with Stimulus Y436 that enraged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:56.940
the ambitious doctor. Expecting the anomalous&nbsp;
stimulant to turn SCP-5683 into a fine mist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:01.860
Kristiansen watched as the creature’s&nbsp;
body vanished, literally vaporizing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:06.660
changing states of matter to little more than&nbsp;
water in the air. Suddenly, every light in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:11.340
facility powered off, plunging the testing chamber&nbsp;
into darkness. When the lights came back on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:18.900
SCP-5683 was standing on all eight legs, right&nbsp;
where it had been mist only three seconds earlier.&nbsp;

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:23.700
The research team had gathered for another&nbsp;
mediation, and Doctor Kristiansen’s anger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:27.900
still hadn’t subsided. He kicked a&nbsp;
chair to emphasize his frustration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:34.200
alarming Junior Researcher Silva, who urged him to&nbsp;
calm down. After eventually, cooling his temper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:39.360
Kristiansen made an announcement that caused&nbsp;
even greater concern to spread among the team.&nbsp;

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:44.400
“I’m requisitioning Y910.”
Researcher Hall and Researcher Miles objected,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:48.900
trying to get Doctor Kristiansen to realize&nbsp;
that this course of action was excessive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:54.960
overkill even. But Kristiansen disregarded them,&nbsp;
standing by his latest method for terminating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:02.640
SCP-5683. The Global Occult Coalition had&nbsp;
previously used Y910 to poison gods, he felt sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:08.460
that it would work on one anomalous giant spider.
His time was running short, Doctor Kristiansen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:14.160
was aware that any day now, the O5 Council would&nbsp;
be appointing a replacement Director of Site 04,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:20.760
and he wanted that promotion. And he didn’t seem&nbsp;
to care what corners he cut – and what risks he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:26.400
took – to get there, even if it meant endangering&nbsp;
his researcher personnel. Doctor Kristiansen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:31.860
declared that, in order to save time, he would&nbsp;
be bypassing tissue sample tests for termination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:36.660
attempts. The longer it took to terminate the&nbsp;
anomalous arachnid, the more his window of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:42.360
opportunity closed and the further the Director&nbsp;
position slipped from his fingertips. Accepting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:47.820
full responsibility for the reckless decision and&nbsp;
anything that might go wrong, Doctor Kristiansen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:55.860
wanted to use Stimulus Y910 directly on SCP-5683.&nbsp;
He urged the research team to make the necessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.860 --> 00:11:02.520
preparations, unaware of what his decision would&nbsp;
lead to… and the chaos it had already caused.&nbsp;

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:09.420
The test was catastrophic. So much so that it&nbsp;
caused a containment breach. With SCP-5683 loose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.420 --> 00:11:14.220
and scuttling about the facility on its multiple&nbsp;
legs, Doctor Kristiansen and Junior Researcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:19.620
Silva were forced to rush to the secure bunker&nbsp;
on site for safety. Kristiansen was in a state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:25.200
of panic, until he noticed something – and not&nbsp;
for the first time, either. He’d been detecting a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:30.480
foul smell whenever he’d conducted the meetings to&nbsp;
discuss termination options. But the other members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:34.980
of the research team had quickly explained it&nbsp;
was nothing more than repeated ‘accidents’ in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:41.160
the cafeteria. But here was the stench again,&nbsp;
worse than ever. Yet, Junior Researcher Silva&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:47.460
brushed it off again, stating SCP-5683&nbsp;
must’ve gotten into the facility’s reactor.&nbsp;

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:52.920
The Junior Researcher quickly became inconsolable,&nbsp;
stating that the whole situation was his fault.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:58.800
Doctor Kristiansen interjected, demanding to&nbsp;
know how it was, and what Silva had done to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:03.780
cause this situation. He replied that it had&nbsp;
been his duty to oppose ill-advised actions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:10.200
and when Kristiansen had declared his intention&nbsp;
to use Y910, the Junior researcher hadn’t opposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:15.360
him. Shifting the blame from himself onto his&nbsp;
subordinate, Doctor Kristiansen chastised Silva&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:19.920
over how many personnel had died because of&nbsp;
the Junior Researcher’s refusal to do his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:25.560
job – ignoring that it was Kristiansen’s own&nbsp;
ambitions that had led to the current chaos.&nbsp;

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:30.600
Refusing to be made a scapegoat, Doctor&nbsp;
Kristiansen vowed to pin the full culpability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:37.260
for SCP-5683’s containment breach onto Junior&nbsp;
Researcher Silva, saying he’d tell the O5&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:42.240
Council the so-called ‘truth’ about what had&nbsp;
happened. But Silva pointed out there wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:47.640
much likely the bunker would survive the reactor&nbsp;
overloading. He urged the ambitions Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:53.280
doctor to admit some responsibility of his own&nbsp;
for what had happened, but Kristiansen refused.&nbsp;

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:58.800
Suddenly, there came a thunderous banging at&nbsp;
the bunker door. A debilitating pang of fear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:04.680
struck Doctor Kristiansen, causing him to scream&nbsp;
and retreat from the entrance, yelling ‘no’ and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:09.660
‘please’ as if he was pleading with the universe&nbsp;
itself to spare him from the spider. Junior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:15.240
Researcher Silva walked over to the bunker door,&nbsp;
just as strong, arachnid legs tore the heavy steel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:22.380
bulkhead off its hinges like it was made of little&nbsp;
more than wet paper. Stood behind was SCP-5683,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:26.520
the enormous spider skittering into&nbsp;
the bunker, screeching all the while.&nbsp;

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:32.940
Silva had put himself between SCP-5683 and&nbsp;
the ambitious Foundation doctor, whose hunger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:38.400
for a promotion had led to all this carnage. The&nbsp;
Junior Researcher announced his noble intention to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:43.920
sacrifice himself, occupying the creature while&nbsp;
he urged Kristiansen to run. The doctor shoved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:50.340
Silva towards the spider and prepared to run…
Then, all of a sudden, SCP-5683 vanished.&nbsp;

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:55.800
Junior Researcher Silva told Doctor Kristiansen&nbsp;
he was disappointed, before Researcher Miles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.800 --> 00:14:01.380
Researcher Hall, and Security Chief Aday all&nbsp;
entered the bunker through the torn-open hole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:08.460
where the door had been. Kristiansen questioned&nbsp;
where SCP-5683 had gone, to which Silva explained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:13.980
there was little reason to keep a dummy around&nbsp;
once it had served its purpose… as a substitute.&nbsp;

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:19.560
“You mentioned you worked with a lizard, sir,”&nbsp;
the Junior Researcher recounted. “That there was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:24.840
a containment breach. If you don't terribly&nbsp;
mind me asking, how did you escape that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:31.260
situation? It seemed quite lethal, didn't it?”
Afraid and confused, Doctor Kristiansen asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:37.380
where he was. Hall and Miles urged him not to ask&nbsp;
questions he already knew the answer to. Silva&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:43.920
explained who they all were: a Jury, specifically&nbsp;
Doctor Kristiansen’s Jury. And according to them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:50.940
the ambitious doctor had disgraced himself again.
Kristiansen had been there for a long time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:59.340
a considerably long time, reliving the same&nbsp;
events over and over again, with SCP-5683&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:06.600
acting as a substitute for SCP-682. It was the&nbsp;
same situation, he’d made the same decisions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:13.560
the same mistakes – and it had cost lives. Now,&nbsp;
Doctor Kristiansen was trapped in an endless loop,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:19.200
penance for the casualties that had occurred at&nbsp;
his hands, all in the pursuit of his own selfish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:25.140
personal gain. He asked the Jury how long he’d be&nbsp;
stuck there, a question Silva responded to with:&nbsp;

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:30.060
“Until you take responsibility, sir.”
Immediately, Doctor Kristiansen tried to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:36.300
admit this had all been his fault. But he didn’t&nbsp;
mean it, not really. He hadn’t accepted blame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:41.820
he just wanted a quick and easy way out of the&nbsp;
loop; and the Jury of his deceased personnel knew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:46.860
it. Kristiansen ran for the door in the hopes&nbsp;
of escaping his fate, futile as his chances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:52.920
were. A black iron chain appeared from around the&nbsp;
corner and wrapped itself around the overambitious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:58.260
doctor’s throat, ignorant of his pleas for&nbsp;
forgiveness. Saying he was sorry wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:03.900
bring back the people who’d died in service&nbsp;
of his aspirations to become a Site Director.&nbsp;

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:09.960
The chain dragged Doctor Kristiansen through the&nbsp;
facility at such a speed that he collided with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:16.500
every wall, and every corner as he turned&nbsp;
sharply, pulled along the floor. But that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:22.440
and the walls quickly crumbled away, revealing a&nbsp;
sight that made Doctor Kristiansen start screaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:27.540
that it wasn’t his fault – and he never&nbsp;
really stopped. What followed involved a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:33.900
great deal of blood and fire. Once it was over,&nbsp;
it left behind the same awful stench the doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:40.200
had smelt before. And he’d soon be smelling&nbsp;
it again too, as the cycle repeated itself.&nbsp;

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:43.980
The directive had come straight&nbsp;
from a member of the O5 Council.&nbsp;

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:49.260
They were impressed with Doctor Kristiansen.
And the ambitious Foundation doctor had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:55.380
hoping to snag a Director position at Site 04.
But there was one final test: for Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.380 --> 00:17:03.420
Kristiansen to solve the SCP-5683 problem.
Now check out “SCP-5000 WHY? - THE FULL&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:09.540
STORY COMPILATION” and “SCP-3023 - AND THEN&nbsp;
IT DECIDED TO BE AN ANGRY SPIDER” for more!

